Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:42:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/49] F3 (M22 test): the directory-state test counts entries
 instead of sampling the heap

Release check F3. TestRestoreKeepsNoPathPerDirectory sampled the live
heap of a running restore and failed in 3 of 20 runs alone on four
CPUs (7 of 15 under load), on the repaired tree as on this one: a
sample also counts what other threads allocated since the collection
began. The flakiness was the test's, not the restore's.

The structure M22 bounds, the set of directories this restore created
itself, is now a field of the Restorer (it was a local of RestoreTo;
same map, same uses). The test counts its entries from SelectFilter,
which runs on the traversal's goroutine for every node of both passes:
at most 3 for a tree three deep, and none after the restore. That is
exact on every platform. Without the M22 repair it reads 3,011 and
12,041.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
